CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=8a08708a-3336bd69-0133-925217ab-00007269:Bazemore\,
  Serena
CREATED:20260921T130501Z
DESCRIPTION:"Jewish Literatures Beyond Zionism" workshop is being held at 
 SUNY-Binghamton.\n\nThis workshop explores contemporary approaches to the
  study of modern Jewish literature\, with particular attention to questio
 ns of identity\, nationalism\, diaspora\, memory\, and transnational lite
 rary exchange. Participants will examine how recent historical and politi
 cal developments have prompted scholars to reconsider established framewo
 rks in Jewish literary studies and to explore alternative interpretive mo
 dels.\n\nBringing together researchers from a range of disciplinary persp
 ectives\, the workshop will address topics such as diasporic Jewish liter
 atures\, comparative minority literatures\, translation and cultural circ
 ulation\, Sephardic and Mizrahi writing\, gender and sexuality\, decoloni
 al methodologies\, and the relationship between literature and social mov
 ements. The workshop aims to foster rigorous scholarly dialogue on the di
 verse histories\, languages\, and futures of Jewish literary cultures.\n\
 nThe Sperling Center for Jewish Studies is proud to co-sponsor this event
  begin held at the Judaic Studies Department at SUNY-Binghamton with the 
 Duke Department of Asian and Middle Eastern Studies.
DURATION:P2D
DTSTAMP:20260921T130501Z
