CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=00f1fcdb-0f068baf-010f-068baf83-00000004:None
CREATED:20260911T145500Z
DESCRIPTION:On October 13\, 2026\, Close Up will lead a regional deliberat
 ion at Duke University. This event is one of six regional deliberations t
 aking place in 2026-27 across the country as part of NextGen Roundtable: 
 America 250\, a growing initiative to honor the Semiquincentennial of the
  United States. Through civil discourse\, we aim to empower students to e
 ngage in meaningful dialogue\, listen with empathy\, and express their id
 eas with clarity and confidence.\n\n\nThis NextGen Roundtable regional de
 liberation will convene up to 250 high school students from public\, char
 ter\, private\, and independent schools in the area\nwho represent a cros
 s-section of backgrounds and perspectives. Students will deliberate on ec
 onomic policy issues in small groups moderated by neutral\nfacilitators\,
  weigh diverse perspectives from their peers and a panel of policy expert
 s\, and craft vision statements for making an impact in their community.\
 nAll participating students will receive Close Up's Deliberative Dialogue
  Badge.\n\nAs students deliberate\, accompanying educators will take part
  in a Close Up-led professional development workshop around deliberative 
 dialogue and\npolitical values\, including an introduction to Close Up's 
 free\, four-week curricular unit\, "Cornerstones of American Democracy\,"
  about how our country's\ncore political values regularly come into tensi
 on. Following the PD session\, educators will earn continuing education u
 nits for applying what they learn in\ntheir classrooms.
DURATION:PT6H
DTSTAMP:20260911T145500Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261013T080000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260911T145500Z
