CREATED:20260629T183322Z
DESCRIPTION:The 2026 Duke-ORNL Workshop on Advanced Microscopy and Data-Dr
 iven Materials Science will be held at Duke University on October 12-13\,
  2026. The workshop will bring together leading researchers\, industry ex
 perts\, and emerging scholars to explore the latest advances in electron 
 microscopy\, AI-enabled data analysis\, and data-driven materials discove
 ry.\n\nThe program will showcase cutting-edge characterization techniques
  and computational approaches for next-generation energy and quantum mate
 rials\, including batteries\, two-dimensional materials\, and complex int
 erfaces. By connecting fundamental research with industrial applications\
 , the workshop will foster collaborations among academia\, national labor
 atories\, and industry while engaging regional industry partners.\n\nStud
 ents and postdoctoral researchers are especially encouraged to participat
 e. The workshop will feature networking opportunities\, career developmen
 t activities\, and a poster session with awards recognizing outstanding s
 tudent and postdoctoral presentations.\n\nBy fostering interdisciplinary 
 dialogue\, the workshop aims to identify new research opportunities and s
 upport the development of the next-generation materials science workforce
 .\n\nWorkshop Information:\n\n• Agenda has been updated! | Visit the webs
 ite: (https://sites.duke.edu/dukeornlworkshop2026/) to review.\n• Registr
 ation is required to attend the workshop (the cost is free). Participants
  will have the option to indicate whether they wish to present a poster d
 uring registration. \n• Invited Speakers | Visit the website (https://sit
 es.duke.edu/dukeornlworkshop2026/) to learn more! \n• Additional Sponsors
 : DECTRIS\, Evident\, JEOL USA\, Inc.\, Gatan\, Inc.\, Duke-ORNL\, Thermo
 Fisherer
DURATION:PT9H
DTSTAMP:20260928T125325Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261013T083000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260928T125325Z
